# Hugging Face settings for this machine only. To use them:
#   cp .env.template .env
# .env is ignored by git, so your token never ends up in the public repo.
#
# Everything here is optional. Without a .env, sync_models.sh downloads the
# public models in models.txt and skips the gated ones.

# Access token, needed only for gated models (marked GATED| in models.txt).
# Create one at https://huggingface.co/settings/tokens ("Read" is enough) and
# accept each gated model's terms on its page first.
#HF_TOKEN=hf_your_token_here

# Which of a model's files to download for vLLM and SGLang: a whitelist, so
# anything not listed is skipped. The default below is what those engines need:
# the weights in .safetensors format, plus the model's small files (settings,
# tokenizer, chat template). It skips older weight formats that can run code
# when they are opened (.bin, .pth), the model's own Python code, GGUF files,
# READMEs and images. Patterns are separated by spaces or commas; "*" downloads
# everything.
#HF_INCLUDE="*.safetensors *.json *.jinja *.model *.txt *.tiktoken"
# The engines never go online, so a file type left out here is missing for
# them. Without *.jinja, for example, most models can't chat.
# Lines with a size (GGUF, for llama.cpp) ignore this and HF_EXCLUDE: they get
# just that size's files, which carry their own tokenizer and chat template.

# Files to skip even when they match the whitelist, e.g. "original/*".
#HF_EXCLUDE=""

# Set to 'true' to hide the progress bars.
#HF_QUIET=false
